data.content:
These are three known C# 13 breaking changes. Here's what breaks and the fixes:

## 1. `Buffer.cs` — `[InlineArray]` on `record struct` is now an error

C# 13 disallows `[InlineArray]` on `record struct` because the compiler-synthesized `Equals`/`GetHashCode` only compare `_element0`, not all elements. Fix: use a plain `struct`.

```csharp
[System.Runtime.CompilerServices.InlineArray(10)]
struct Buffer
{
    private int _element0;
}
```

## 2. `Generator.cs` — `stackalloc` in local functions inside iterators

C# 13 now considers local functions within iterators as part of the iterator state machine, so `stackalloc` is disallowed there. Fix: extract it to a separate `static` method.

```csharp
unsafe class DataGenerator
{
    IEnumerable<int> Generate()
    {
        yield return 1;
        Process();
    }

    static void Process()
    {
        int* p = stackalloc int[10];
        // ... work with pointer
    }
}
```

## 3. `Resolver.cs` — Overload resolution ambiguity with `[]`

C# 13 expanded collection-expression conversions to `Span<T>` and `ReadOnlySpan<T>`, so `[]` now matches **both** overloads, causing an ambiguity error. Fix: cast explicitly.

```csharp
static void Main()
{
    Process((ReadOnlySpan<int>)[]);
}
```
